kals: the Kairo language server.

    python3 build.py --debug kals        # build/<triple>/debug/bin/kals
    python3 Analyzer/Dev/smoke.py        # end-to-end check over stdio

Design, file formats and the compiler hooks: Compiler/Spec/LanguageServer.md.

Where the code is
-----------------
Driver/kals.k                    main: `kals` is the server, `kals --worker` one analysis
Protocol.k                       wire constants: methods, error codes, kinds, LSP enums
Tuning.k                         every tunable (debounces, limits, caps), with its trade-off
JsonRpc.k, kals_io.h             Content-Length framing over stdin/stdout
Json.k                           JSON reader (flat document) and writer
DocumentStore.k                  open buffers, incremental edits, UTF-16 positions
TextScan.k                       brackets and comment runs: folding, selection, signature help
Workspace/CompileCommandsLoader.k  kairo_compile.json

Server/  one class, Server, split over `extend Server` files
  Server.k                       state, the loop, the message router, server_main
  Output.k                       respond, notify, request, log, trace, progress
  Lifecycle.k                    project file, initialize, capabilities
  Scheduling.k                   Job / Entry / Parked, which entry holds a file, parking
  Workers.k                      worker argv, launch, reap, installing a snapshot
  Diagnostics.k                  publishing; the per-keystroke syntax pass
  Lookup.k                       reading snapshot rows: ref_at, nth, uses
  Features.k                     hover, definition, references, highlights, links, inlays, rename
  Tokens.k                       semantic tokens: full, delta, range
  Structure.k                    document symbols, folding, selection, workspace symbols
  CodeActions.k                  quick fixes, macro expansion, generate interface
  Navigation.k                   call / type hierarchy, code lens
  SignatureHelp.k, Formatting.k, Completion.k
  ClangdBridge.k                 generated headers and clangd's overlay for C/C++ sources
  TextUtil.k                     text helpers (search, case, top-level names, keywords)

Index/   the worker side
  Worker.k                       the worker: overlays, the compile, diagnostics as LSP JSON
  Indexer.k                      IndexWalker: state, classification, the visits
  Legend.k                       token types and modifiers (positions, bits, names)
  Snapshot.k                     row types and their column constants (REF_*, BASE_*, ...)
  Writer.k                       writes the snapshot in Snapshot.k's column order
  Tokens.k, Refs.k, Hovers.k, CompletionItems.k, Bases.k, Inlays.k, Macros.k
                                 the walker's parts, as `extend IndexWalker`

Dev/                             lsp_client.py (a scripted client), smoke.py (the test),
                                 bench.py (the cost rules: edits, row lookups)

The editor clients (VS Code, Zed, Neovim) are in the kairo-lsp repository.
